\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 1. Why tools exist\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 CineBot now has a brain that always answers in a fixed structure. It still has no hands.\
Asked "Is Interstellar showing tonight at 7pm at the downtown cinema?", the model replied that it has no access to live listings and suggested Googling it. Wrap the same question in 
\f2\fs26 with_structured_output
\f1\fs24  and it fills the schema fields with nothing useful, or invents a showtime.\
The model is limited to what it knows. Anything outside that \'97 live data, a database, an external API, an action in the world \'97 needs a tool.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Tools are just glorified API calls or functions. If you can't write a proper function, you won't write a good tool.\
Anytime an agent needs to reach outside itself, it goes through a tool. MCP, covered later, is essentially a collection of tools.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 2. Defining a tool\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 from langchain_core.tools import tool\
\
@tool\
def check_showtimes(movie_title: str) -> str:\
    """Get the showtimes for a given movie."""\
    return f"\{movie_title\} is showing at 4pm, 7pm and 10pm"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

